    "created_at": "2016-09-28T14:14:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-28T14:14:26Z",
    "body": "FWIW, we could check sandboxing on \"this Document object's relevant global object's Document object\" and also modify the origin there and use that for the `domain` getter, but it seems user agents are inconsistent so I need some guidance from implementers as what they'd like to do here. \n\nMaking it a no-op and always returning the empty string when it's not a document associated with a browsing context still seems preferable to me, but whatever.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
